World data and composition contracts (@ws-contract-world-composition: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @workspace-contracts, #requires @ws-world-composition, #requires @ws-offline-city, #requires @ws-scene-reconstruction, #requires @ws-generated-scenes, #requires @ws-live-scene-reconstruction) { r_0WN3E2KGPRM730VC1FHMRM30F9
Owner refinement, 2026-11-20. A world representation is curated, revisioned data. Begin with a cheap flat map, coarse globe or fictional scene, improve selected parts with supplied, measured, reconstructed, generated and authored data, and retain those improvements across detail changes and source refresh. The same model, frame, source, query, editing and package interfaces serve a home, workplace, city, invented world or extracted fragment. The capability is generic; geographic examples and inspiring games supply evidence and fixtures.

[Development graph](../Workspace-Development.lingua) · [Implementation owner](../features/World-Composition.lingua)

## Existing contracts and ownership

Reuse Frames R0132–R0144 for units, CRS, datums and independent roots. Reuse the shared source/product envelope in R0473 and Assets 05.T04a. Offline city 06.T01 owns actual geographic ingestion and R0494–R0497 owns coverage/source metadata and permitted acquisition. Imports 09.T01–09.T03 owns base layering, registration and source updates. Simplification and Navigation own collision/support products and walking. Assets 06.T05 owns portable Workspace export. [Frames](Frames-and-views-contracts.lingua) · [Shared source contracts](Scale-navigation-and-hosting-contracts.lingua) · [Offline coverage](Offline-coverage-contracts.lingua) · [Imported bases](Imported-base-contracts.lingua)

[World composition](../features/World-Composition.lingua) first delivers local alignment, regional replacement, curation and fragments after Imports, on WC.F02. This contract joins it with actual Offline city geographic acquisition, [Scene reconstruction](../features/Scene-Reconstruction.lingua), [Generated scenes](../features/Generated-Scenes.lingua) and [Live reconstruction](../features/Live-Scene-Reconstruction.lingua). The bounded creation methods are explicit deliverables with real execution proofs. Base Observed models retains its earlier independent 2D/proxy proof.

The shared boundary is input sources → implemented method → versioned model candidate → alignment/review → ordinary layer or region replacement. WCO.T02 owns it through existing jobs/products/accepted operations. Reconstruction and generation may proceed in independent leaf modules after that export; shared worker, schema and publication changes remain serialized. Live reconstruction additionally requires actual camera/vision exports. This contract joins core acceptance through 15.T11/15.W10. The isolated direct-Bevy Kamalie Castle remains an independent first game milestone.

## Required outcomes

- [ ] **WC.M01.** Select a bounded real place or supplied dataset and inspect available source layers, dates, quality, costs and missing coverage. Ingest supported semantic/vector, terrain and appearance inputs through actual adapters.
- [ ] **WC.M02.** Compose a recognizable scene with stable source correspondence, measured/estimated distinctions and explicit property/purpose conflict resolution. Inspect one feature's contributing sources and derivation.
- [ ] **WC.M03.** Walk a declared supported route with useful collision and clearance while visual detail changes, preserving gaps and unsupported interiors.
- [ ] **WC.M04.** Edit a local structure, update a source and reconcile the change while preserving authored placement, identity and normal undo.
- [ ] **WC.M05.** Save a permitted visual/edit/walk profile as ordinary Workspace data, reopen it offline and place another instance in an independent local composition through the same loader and frame services.

- [ ] **WC.M06.** Improve a supplied coarse scene through native alignment and partial replacement, including overlapping refinements, safe boundaries, coherent distant summaries and preserved mounted components. Repeat on a fictional root with geographic services inactive.
- [ ] **WC.M07.** Curate accepted revisions, inspect contributing evidence, reconcile source updates and extract/rebase an arbitrary supported fragment for reuse as an instance or independent editable copy.
- [ ] **WC.M08.** Produce actual model candidates from overlapping supplied photographs, image-plus-terrain inputs and one implemented AI generation method, then adopt and reopen their permitted outputs through ordinary Workspace operations.
- [ ] **WC.M09.** Produce one-shot and periodic detailed candidates from a supported live-camera method with volatile inputs, per-source calibration/time, bounded accumulated geometry and no raw-media archive.

## Requirements

- [ ] **WC.R01.** Produce the shared model/source/product envelope with optional geographic association, declared local frame and bounded dependencies. Earth coordinates are interpreted by the selected geographic adapter. The common loader, model and composition services accept ordinary local roots. A place can be attached to Earth, opened alone or instanced in a fictional scene while retaining source identity and canonical dimensions. Presentation scale/placement and geographic association have separate owners.
- [ ] **WC.R02.** Preserve dataset/provider identity, upstream feature IDs, revision, capture versus publication time, extent, resolution, accuracy/uncertainty, units, horizontal CRS, vertical datum, epoch when relevant, no-data masks, attribution, access and permitted uses. State whether heights describe bare terrain, roofs/vegetation surfaces, absolute elevation, height above ground or levels. Derived products retain transform and source lineage down to their meaningful feature/patch scope.
- [ ] **WC.R03.** Support bounded source discovery by region, time, desired product and provider capability. Show available coverage before acquisition, estimate encoded/decoded/processing cost and use existing admission, paging, download and job controls. User-supplied local sources use the same downstream path. Unknown coverage stays unknown. Source authentication and current access/export policy apply to discovery as well as payload retrieval. A larger catalogue increases addressable coverage through sparse indexes and demand-driven acquisition.
- [ ] **WC.R04.** Publish an actual supported adapter matrix. First acceptance includes semantic building/road vector data with IDs and tags, a georeferenced terrain raster with a documented height meaning, and a registered appearance input such as an orthophoto or textured mesh. Select concrete decoder variants and capture bounded fixtures before implementation. GeoJSON/OSM extracts, GeoTIFF/COG and glTF/GLB are initial candidates. Overture GeoParquet, LAS/LAZ/COPC, CityJSON/CityGML, 3D Tiles and splat variants remain separately declared capabilities until real import, loss and resource proofs exist. Preserve source fields needed for later geometry and queries through the existing normalization path.
- [ ] **WC.R05.** A composition recipe pins input manifests, transforms and their offline resources, source-selection masks, property/purpose preferences, derivation operators, parameters, software versions and any random seed. Run through existing bounded jobs and generation-checked publication. Rebuild affected products incrementally, keep the previous valid view during replacement, and inspect why a product changed. Every advertised operator has an implemented native execution path and a supported input/output schema.
- [ ] **WC.R06.** Associate evidence using upstream identity where available and explicit spatial/semantic matches otherwise. Store ambiguous associations and source alternatives. Select authority by property and purpose, considering accuracy, capture time, coverage and provenance. A newer appearance layer can coexist with an older surveyed support model. Detect overlapping duplicates and define replace/mask/additive behavior for competing geometry. Show registration residuals and withheld checks. Preserve authored fixed placement under Q17 when terrain or surveys change.
- [ ] **WC.R07.** Missing geometry follows R0495 until a source or explicit authoring supplies it. An optional completion profile may derive extrusion from supported heights, estimate height from floors with a declared assumption, choose a roof form or add plausible decorative detail. Store those choices, uncertainty and lineage in a switchable derived/authored layer. Estimated interiors, vegetation, street furniture and AI-generated geometry carry their actual origin. Users can replace a completion with stronger evidence and reconcile affected products.
- [ ] **WC.R08.** Keep semantic features, visible geometry/materials and collision/support independently usable. Any supplied or implemented route graph, navmesh or route-solving product has its own declared provider capability and evidence under R0497. The first walking proof uses the existing local support-query path. A road centerline needs width/surface/access information or declared authored assumptions before generating a walkable road. A terrain heightfield needs separate bridge/underpass geometry for stacked surfaces. Point clouds, imagery, photogrammetry and splats require actual geometric support before movement relies on them. Walking validates slope, step, clearance and supported openings. Report unseen interiors and missing support explicitly.
- [ ] **WC.R09.** Use independent visual, structural, behavioral and computational policies. Cheap buildings can retain source identity and semantic queries while detailed facades unload. Keep a bounded movement-support neighborhood ahead of the player and apply safe support replacement. Aggregate geometry and instances by useful spatial/material groups with source correspondence. Budgets include textures, decode/upload, solver/support, labels, queues and active CPU work. A photographically convincing view is evaluated separately from metric accuracy and walkability.
- [ ] **WC.R10.** Source refresh uses captured revisions and coherent manifest publication through existing reimport and acceptance paths. Handle renames, splits, deletion, access changes and unresolved correspondences. Concurrent authored edits survive stale completion. Separate capture dates on overlapping layers remain visible. Cancellation/retry uses existing job identity and bounded cleanup, including processing scratch and partially acquired source chunks.
- [ ] **WC.R11.** Export a chosen purpose profile through the existing .lince-workspace directory/packed format and dependency-closure validator. Include required models, assets, transforms, materials, styles, semantic data, support products and attributions that can be distributed for that profile. Report restricted, omitted and unavailable inputs and the resulting capability/quality loss. A service-backed view declares its external dependency and the offline fallback it can actually supply. Preserve source-specific terms through derived products and package updates.
- [ ] **WC.R12.** Camera feeds and Fiote observations contribute time-stamped derived layers through the existing Camera/Vision/Observed Models contracts. Static scene publication preserves the observation's capture window, uncertainty and output lineage. Scene age and observed changes remain distinct from simulated activity. The camera contract retains bounded transient media and its existing no-archive scope. Live-Scene-Reconstruction owns an actual bounded higher-detail method and its measured support. The basic observed 2D/proxy proof remains independent; a schema slot cannot satisfy detailed reconstruction.
- [ ] **WC.R13.** Native controls expose region/source selection, layer purpose, coverage, source conflicts, estimated completion, preview/cancel/adopt, walkability and package export. Share accepted operations and receipts with later Fiote integration. Source and layer inspection remain useful through table/2D views. Preserve readable controls, normal undo, existing mounts and edit-panel-geometry. Selecting or loading a geographic package uses the same ordinary Workspace content entry points as other models.
- [ ] **WC.R14.** Report at least six independent quality dimensions for the chosen place/profile, covering metric alignment, visual resemblance, semantic completeness, capture freshness, traversable coverage and runtime cost. Pin reference points, known dimensions, expected routes, masks and source dates before inspecting outputs. Record achieved resolution and source accuracy separately. A high-detail asset can improve one dimension while leaving others unknown.

- [ ] **WC.R15 — Three distinct placements.** Preserve the source frame/units and optional geospatial association, the measured or estimated registration into a model frame, and each occurrence's placement in its destination. Known CRS/datum/epoch transformations use an actual adapter and pinned resources. Otherwise expose translate/rotate, numeric position/orientation, known length/scale and control-point alignment, with residuals and withheld checks. Disclose unsolved degrees of freedom; a single point is not a complete rigid alignment. Preview the transform before acceptance. Reusing a real fragment in a fictional root preserves provenance without forcing its destination to be Earth. Presentation magnification remains separate from physical resizing.
- [ ] **WC.R16 — Regional refinement operation.** A refinement identifies destination root/occurrence and captured revision, region selector/frame, source candidate/revision, affected purposes/layers, Add/Overlay/Replace mode, priority, seam policy and dependency versions. First selectors are explicit objects/subobjects and a planar footprint with vertical interval; state anchor-membership versus occupied-volume overlap. Preview all affected contributors before applying. The operation has ordinary undo and accepted revision history. Higher priority is explicit, with ties reported deterministically. Replacement can target an imported base while retaining a user-authored house, panel or behavior layer. A visual mask never silently disables collision, semantics or behavior.
- [ ] **WC.R17 — Honest cuts and boundaries.** Whole-object replacement, source-layer spatial masking and actual geometry clipping are distinct supported operations. Implement bounded polygon/terrain/triangle-mesh cuts through Geometry and preserve their source correspondence; show open boundaries and whether a supported cap was authored. Do not call an open mesh a closed solid. Other representations advertise their actual mask/clipping variants. Separate appearance blend, terrain edge stitching and support continuity: blending pixels does not close a walking gap. Reconcile height/edge samples for supported terrain seams, validate overlap/double surfaces and expose roads, bridge decks and openings requiring an authored transition. Arbitrary watertight joining of unrelated meshes/splats is not assumed.
- [ ] **WC.R18 — Coherent replacement.** Keep the previous accepted revision while products stage. Validate the intended combination of geometry, appearance, semantic mappings and support before switching its manifest. Different purposes may intentionally use different sources, with the chosen policy visible. On failure, cancellation or stale target, retain the old state and offer repair or a separately saved candidate. Active movement uses the existing safe support handoff, including an explicit stop/relocation policy where needed; never switch to absent support. Account for old/new transient residency and revoke unneeded jobs/products after undo or replacement.
- [ ] **WC.R19 — References survive refinement.** Source IDs and lineage survive reordering/retiling/LOD; occurrences and independent copies retain their own identities under R0120–R0126/R0147–R0154. Picks carry representation revision and delayed picks are revalidated or rejected. Preserve selection, annotations and mounts through proven correspondence; splits/deletions expose unresolved repair. Q17 keeps fixed authored pose stable. An ambiguous wall successor cannot teleport a mounted app, and replacement does not capture focus or duplicate its producer. Behavior bindings and external controls change only through their accepted operations.
- [ ] **WC.R20 — Detail preserves accepted content.** Apply R0488–R0489 to every regional refinement: publish changed bounds/coarse proxies, invalidate affected summaries and retain masks/priority through paging, save/reload and offline use. Lower visual detail may simplify the new house; it cannot reveal the superseded base house or erase the accepted edit. Visual, structural, behavior/simulation and computational policies remain independent. A camera appearance upgrade does not activate physics or prove structural detail. Query provenance and selected identity remain available at cheap detail. Rebuild only affected spatial/dependency paths.
- [ ] **WC.R21 — Care over time.** Keep source revisions immutable and local corrections in normal editable layers. Show the accepted head, author/origin, capture age, contributing evidence and dirty/stale derivations; provide compare, pin/follow, accept/reject update and undo through existing history. Explicitly authorized periodic derived updates may advance their own layer while preserving authored overrides. Pin, following and offline retention are separate choices. Resolve source conflicts property by property where supported. Source loss or permission change reports gaps and permitted retained fallback. Unknown/occluded areas remain distinguishable from observed absence; an attractive generated patch cannot acquire measured status by merging.
- [ ] **WC.R22 — Extract and reuse fragments.** Select objects or a supported region, choose whole-object versus actual crop, and preview closure/cut boundaries. Produce a model/package with required geometry, textures/atlases, materials, semantics, support, transforms, source IDs, lineage and attributions. Closure follows references, including dependencies outside the crop; if those cannot be exported, derive a permitted subset or report the missing capability. Rebase into a chosen local frame while preserving canonical dimensions and original association. Place instance shares the selected definition/revision with independent occurrence placement; Make editable copy creates an independent definition retaining lineage. Choose destination environment bindings under R0131/Q15, applying gravity once. No city, geographic hierarchy or global-service dependency is mandatory for local use.
- [ ] **WC.R23 — Common creation candidate.** Extend the existing source/product/job envelopes with actual method/operator and version/checkpoint, input IDs/revisions and retention class, capture/window metadata, calibration and transforms, constraints/parameters/seed where supported, budgets, declared output types, bounds/coverage, scale status and per-patch/property provenance. Candidate outputs include editable source/recipe where available, geometry/appearance/semantics and separately validated support, dependency closure, uncertainty/residuals, unknown masks and capability/loss report. A candidate can exist in its own local frame without a target. An optional adoption target pins root/layer/region/authority/revision and is checked again on apply. Support local workers and explicitly configured remote providers through existing admission/credentials/job paths. Implement progress, inspect, cancel, compare and adoption; data types alone cannot complete a method. Exact replay is advertised only when retained inputs and method determinism actually permit it.
- [ ] **WC.R24 — Real methods and input honesty.** First bounded deliverables are supplied mesh placement; polygon/height procedural construction; overlapping supplied-photo reconstruction to geometry; registered imagery draped on known terrain; one real AI generation method yielding editable scene data; and one supported live reconstruction method. Each pins an implemented adapter, format/model versions, input prerequisites, output/loss limits and independently chosen quality controls. A lone satellite image supplies appearance unless a specific depth inference method is invoked and labeled. Metric photo scale needs measured distance/control or suitable calibrated evidence. Stereo satellite height recovery needs its actual sensor/RPC/multi-image adapter. Gaussian splats supply an appearance representation with their own fitting/rendering adapter; collision/support requires separate geometric proof. None is a universal photo-to-perfect-city operation.
- [ ] **WC.R25 — Supplied media versus live windows.** Supplied photographs/scans follow their explicit asset retention/access profile. Camera-derived inputs obey CV.R04 throughout acquisition, synchronization, worker/subprocess scratch, logging and GPU/CPU lifetimes: bounded volatile windows with no raw-frame/video archive or disk spill. A standard worker writing image workspaces is suitable for permitted supplied photos, and needs a verified volatile adapter before live use. Persist permitted derived models, method settings and source/time metadata; expired input makes exact replay unavailable. Stop/revoke/calibration-generation changes fence in-flight work and release leases. Periodic modeling bounds accumulated geometry as well as input buffers.
- [ ] **WC.R26 — City scale through ordinary data.** Use sparse indexes, spatial chunks/levels and demand-driven products from Assets/Geography, including independent source identity across tile splits. A large supplied city model must be converted/indexed incrementally with bounded staging, or rejected with a useful admitted-size limit; opening it never requires decoding the entire city. Precompute/store permitted coarse products and refine only selected demand. Run the same edit/replace/extract operation on a home and a larger multi-tile neighborhood. Measure changed-region rebuild work, addressable versus active content, moving support neighborhood, cancellation and old/new peaks. A whole globe is sparse addressable data with honest coverage, not a claim that fine data exists everywhere.

## Concrete native workflow

1. Open an existing coarse scene in flat or spatial view. Select a place or draw a footprint; Add data offers supported supplied models, available sources, photos, imagery/terrain or a generation job.
2. Inspect the candidate's coverage and origin. Align from valid coordinates, known scale or matching points; use ordinary move/rotate/numeric controls for adjustments. Resolve missing units and inspect residuals before applying.
3. Choose Add, Overlay or Replace region and the affected layers/purposes. Compare old/new appearance, semantic mappings and support. Preview boundaries, conflicts and affected mounted content.
4. Apply through normal acceptance. Keep the coarse overview useful while fine products arrive. Walk where support is validated, edit locally and inspect contributing evidence. Undo or compare an older accepted revision.
5. Refresh a source through reconciliation, or authorize periodic updates to its derived layer. Extract a chosen fragment, rebase it and place it in another workspace as an instance or editable copy.

Creation methods use the same result/review path. Ordinary placement requires no creation worker or AI provider. Advanced source/model controls expand from these actions; edit-panel-geometry preserves the panel flush to the usable left edge and full available height above the bottom-left workspace controls, with reachable controls on narrow viewports.

## Candidate data and tools

Porto Alegre publishes digital-map downloads and a metadata catalogue, including 2010 aerial-survey material. These are discovery starting points. Implementation must pin the exact terrain/building/imagery products, their current access and terms, and their capture dates. The game credit's LiDAR reference alone does not establish public availability of every raw point-cloud product. [Municipal map catalogue](https://www.prefeitura.poa.br/smamus/planejamento-urbano/mapas-digitais) · [Municipal metadata catalogue](https://gis-smamus.portoalegre.rs.gov.br/geonetwork/srv/search)

OSM supplies geographic features and tags. Overture's building theme combines footprints and building parts, with optional height information and source metadata. Height and completeness vary across sources. Preserve the available information and quality gaps when producing geometry. [Overture buildings](https://docs.overturemaps.org/guides/buildings/) · [Building schema](https://docs.overturemaps.org/schema/reference/buildings/building/)

Reusable open tools include OSM2World for generating models from OSM with glTF/GLB and 3D Tiles outputs, and OpenDroneMap for permitted aerial images into textured models, point clouds, orthophotos and elevation products. Arnis provides a further example of real-world geographic data becoming playable world content. Evaluate a bounded tool adapter and its output losses before selecting a production dependency. [OSM2World](https://github.com/tordanik/OSM2World) · [OpenDroneMap](https://github.com/OpenDroneMap/ODM) · [Arnis](https://github.com/louis-e/arnis)

3D Tiles provides a delivery format for large geospatial content, and CityJSON carries semantic city models. Data availability, reconstruction quality, physical support and portable rights remain properties of the supplied dataset and implemented adapters. [OGC 3D Tiles](https://www.ogc.org/standards/3dtiles/) · [OGC CityJSON](https://www.ogc.org/standards/cityjson/)

Provider terms affect the portable-data goal. Google's Map Tiles policy restricts extraction, derived models and caching/export beyond expressly permitted uses. Treat a supported licensed service view according to its actual agreement, and use datasets with suitable reuse rights for portable scene production. Code, input data and style/texture assets can have different licenses. [Google Map Tiles policy](https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/tile/policies) · [Overture attribution](https://docs.overturemaps.org/attribution/)

## Fixtures and acceptance

### WC.F01 — Bounded real place and independent control scene

Choose a bounded locality with usable semantic/vector, measured elevation and permitted appearance sources, varied terrain and recognizable structures. Pin exact coverage, source revisions, terms and losses before implementation. Selection follows available evidence and repeatability; no particular city/provider is required. Porto Alegre can be a useful supplied example when its chosen products are available. Missing products remain missing or use an explicitly identified alternative with declared losses.

Include one authored landmark or correction, one missing patch and one deliberately conflicting source revision. Choose independent control points/dimensions and a finite walking route. A small controlled local fixture supplies a known bridge/underpass and opening when the real source lacks them, with authored lineage visible. The controlled case proves the operator. The real case reports only achieved real coverage.

Repeat composition and portable reopening on a supplied local fictional scene with the geographic profile inactive. Instance the real-place output as ordinary local content with its source metadata intact. The test includes two views and demand release, and an intentionally excluded service-backed layer whose offline fallback is inspected.

### WC.F02 — Coarse local world and nested refinements

Supply a small fictional flat/terrain scene, simple home/workplace blocks, a more detailed textured model with deliberately wrong axes/units, known measured controls, a bridge/opening, a native mounted panel and an unrelated authored object. Prepare overlapping home/neighborhood selectors, split/deleted source revisions and a fragment crossing tile/texture/source boundaries. Record independent expected identities, dimensions and seam/support conditions before running the implementation. No geographic provider is active. WCO's local forms of WC.W01–WC.W05 use these supplied source layers rather than geographic discovery.

Creation owners pin their own bounded photo/terrain/AI/live fixtures and independent checks, then deliver real output into this scene. Extend the geographic fixture with a sparse city-sized index and a declared bounded populated route to measure paging without implying missing city coverage exists. Pin total versus active size and budgets before timed checks.

### WC.W01 — Acquire and explain the place

Select the locality/supplied sources, inspect available coverage/cost/rights, choose actual supported layers, acquire with cancel/resume, and inspect one building's source IDs, height meaning, transform, derivation and uncertainty. Compare chosen evidence against the known control data. Exercise a missing/denied source without losing the current usable scene.

### WC.W02 — Compose appearance and walkable support

Compose terrain, buildings, appearance and the authored detailed asset. Enable and disable explicit estimated completion. Walk the supported route and controlled bridge/opening, switch visual detail and inspect contact/source identity. Verify safe behavior at a support gap. Record resemblance, dimensional residuals, clearance and traversable coverage separately.

### WC.W03 — Edit and refresh

Edit a selected structure and place a native component at a fixed pose. Refresh terrain/building sources with renamed/split/deleted features and changed capture times. Inspect conflict review, preserve the authored edit and fixed placement, test a declared surface-follow attachment and reject stale publication after concurrent edits. Undo through the normal accepted operation path.

### WC.W04 — Package and reuse

Choose the visual/edit/walk profile, inspect its permitted closure and losses, export and reopen with workspace networking disabled. Use the scene as an independent root and as an instance inside the fictional composition. Inspect the same feature through a table and a spatial view. Verify consistent identity, physical dimensions, transform resources, source dates, attribution and supported movement.

### WC.W05 — Bound failure and resource use

Exercise rapid travel, missing fine tiles, overlapping views, malformed inputs, invalid CRS/height interpretation, wrong datum, source replacement, cancel/retry and denied dependencies. Check conservative fallback and safe support publication. Close views and end activity demand, verifying release of decoded/GPU/scratch resources while retaining selected durable packages and edits.

### WC.W06 — Align and refine a region

On WC.F02, add the detailed home, repair its axes/scale, align by control points and inspect withheld residuals. Preview Add/Overlay/Replace, target only selected base purposes and preserve the mounted panel/unrelated authored content. Replace the larger overlapping neighborhood, choose priority, inspect a terrain transition/open boundary and undo/reapply. Walk the supported seam, change visual detail, zoom out/in, evict/reload base tiles and reopen. The accepted home remains represented and discoverable at its meaningful projected scales.

### WC.W07 — Extract and transplant

Extract a fragment crossing tile/texture/source boundaries. Preview whole-object versus crop and dependency closure, choose a local frame and reopen the permitted package offline as its own root. Place it twice inside a fictional world, edit one occurrence placement, then fork one definition and edit its structure independently. Check canonical dimensions, source lineage, semantic queries, support, cut boundaries and exactly-once destination environment bindings. Repeat with a real-place fragment from WC.F01.

### WC.W08 — Curate and repair over time

Compare accepted revisions, pin one source and follow another. Refresh changed geometry while a mounted panel, delayed pick, selection and authored placement edit exist. Check revalidated picks, fixed-pose preservation, explicit ambiguous attachment repair and property-specific source authority. Interrupt generation, revoke a source and reject a stale replacement. Keep permitted last-valid data usable, retain provenance/unknown masks and inspect rebuild scope and undo.

### WC.W09 — Reconstruct from supplied evidence

Run RCN's actual overlapping-photo pipeline and actual image-plus-terrain workflow through native controls. Compare geometry against withheld dimensions/views, inspect unobserved regions, scale recovery, image/elevation alignment and a deliberately missing/wrong-datum terrain input. Review the candidates, align/replace a selected region, edit and reopen outputs offline. Record actual method/version, input retention, quality and computation; an imported precomputed result alone does not prove reconstruction.

### WC.W10 — Generate editable content

Run GEN's actual chosen AI provider on a bounded scene/asset request and any supported references. Validate constraints, inspect generated origin/unknown physical claims, correct dimensions and edit accepted geometry/recipe controls. Use the candidate in a fictional scene and as an explicitly authored alternative at a real place. Cancel/retry and change the target during generation; no late overwrite occurs. Reopen the permitted generated data without rerunning the provider. A deterministic hand-authored fixture cannot substitute for the real model execution.

### WC.W11 — Maintain a region from live observations

Run LRC's actual supported higher-detail camera method once and periodically, producing at least two changed outputs from changed inputs. Inspect calibration, coverage, uncertainty and capture age, adopt into a designated derived layer and preserve authored overrides. Exercise mismatched cameras, moved calibration, occlusion, lost input, cancellation and late completion. Audit bounded media/scratch lifetimes and accumulated geometry; save derived products and metadata without raw media. Exact replay of expired inputs remains unavailable. Basic CV.W01–CV.W05 remains the independently delivered earlier proof.

### WC.W12 — Extend from a local patch to city coverage

Open the declared city-sized sparse fixture to a useful coarse view, travel a bounded populated route and refine only selected neighborhood demand. Replace/extract a multi-tile region through the same controls. Confirm no per-addressed-feature live ECS entity/mesh/collider and no full-city decode to open or edit a home. Measure active set versus addressed coverage, paging, cancellation, support residency, changed-region invalidation and two-view demand release. Report unavailable fine coverage honestly and retain the selected local corrections offline.

### WC.P01 — Correctness and quality

Recover provider evidence and replay WC.W01–WC.W12 through actual native/loader/job paths. WCO publishes its WC.F02/W01–W08 local subset first; the complete contract joins geographic and actual creation-method evidence. Map M01–M05 to W01–W05/W12, M06 to W06/W08, M07 to W07/W08, M08 to W09/W10 and M09 to W11. Retain the creation packages' owned method tests and CV basic proof. Compare independently chosen control dimensions, held-out alignment, semantic correspondence and routes. Record qualitative review of recognizable places and understandable source/conflict controls. Capture the six quality dimensions and actual supported formats/operators. Preserve the existing default missing-data and authored-placement contracts.

### WC.P02 — Cost and offline evidence

Measure catalogue/query size versus active features, encoded/decoded/source/derived bytes, texture and support residency, queue/decode/upload peaks, rebuild scope, frame/input latency and last-demand release on a named device/profile. Compare cold/warm/offline use and two views. Verify zero source/session requests during explicit offline reopening. Repeat the independent local-root case through the same services and include resource costs for processing/replacement overlap.

## Bah City research and transferable approach

Research checked on 2026-11-20. Bah City's official credits identify OpenStreetMap map data, OSM/Overture establishments and Porto Alegre SMAMUS LiDAR 2010 for heights and terrain. The studio describes automatic city assembly from OSM with standardized storefront presentation and individually prepared upgrades. [Game credits](https://bahcity.jogada.studio/game/) · [Studio description](https://bahcity.jogada.studio/vitrine?de=jogo)

The studio reports thirteen neighborhoods reviewed against street imagery and eighty-four landmarks modeled individually. These are published production claims. Their exact source-processing scripts and measured reconstruction accuracy remain undisclosed in the inspected material. [Official press release](https://bahcity.jogada.studio/bah-city-press-release.pdf)

Inspection of the publicly delivered client found Three.js r186, Rapier, spatially packed terrain/building data and worker-generated geometry/collision from polygon rings, height and roof/facade parameters. The inspected manifest used a local geographic-to-meter frame and 256-unit chunks. This supports a pipeline of source ingestion, spatial packaging, generated ordinary geometry and authored detailed replacements. Those implementation details describe the inspected build. [Delivered client](https://bahcity.jogada.studio/assets/index-V3OI6UM0.js) · [Map manifest](https://bahcity.jogada.studio/data/manifest.json) · [Tile worker](https://bahcity.jogada.studio/assets/tileWorker-B8VzL0j-.js)

No official public game repository or reusable game-code license was found in the studio/game pages, press material, delivered assets or matching repository searches. Open-source availability remains unconfirmed. Lince can implement the evidenced data/composition approach using its own runtime and suitable open tools, with source assets carrying their own terms.

The transferable product idea is broad, cheap geographic coverage refined by measured geometry, local corrections and distinctive detailed assets. In Lince those products become reusable model data, usable for inspection, authoring, games and other activities.

Current outcome is unbuilt and unverified. This contract closes after local refinement, geographic composition, the named bounded creation methods and their joined workflows pass. Wider coverage, new format variants and additional methods retain their own measured capability entries. The inspiring game is research context; all implementation owners above expose ordinary reusable Workspace capabilities.
